course: dictionary
lesson: 2514
title: Decide: choosing and settling
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Decide» can mean to make up your mind after thinking, or to settle something so the result is clear. Read the words around it to find which meaning fits. «I decided to stay.» Here you chose after thinking.
explain: «One goal decided the game.» Here decide means settle: the goal made the result clear. Try your meaning in the sentence. Does «choose after thinking» fit here? No, so the other meaning is right.
explain: Decide changes its form: decides, decided, deciding. The noun is «decision», the choice you make. «Deciding what to eat» means choosing what to eat.
explain: Context helps with hard sentences too. «The size of the hole decides which birds can use it» means the size settles which birds can use it. The clue is the word «which»: it tells you the hole settles a choice.
fact: Decide is a verb: decide, decides, decided, deciding.
fact: «Decide» means to make up your mind, to choose after thinking.
fact: «Decide» can also mean to settle something, to make the result clear.
fact: The noun is «decision», which is the choice you make.
fact: In a story, when a character decides what to do, the plot moves on.
exercise: «First decide: coming together or going away?» What does decide mean in this maths sentence? | Add two numbers together | Measure the length of a line | *Choose after thinking | Rub out the answer
exercise: «One goal decided the game.» What does decided mean here? | Scored a goal for the other team | *Made the result clear | Asked the referee a question | Stopped the game for a rest
exercise: Ella asks for the noun from decide, the choice you make. Which word is it? | deciding | decides | decided | *decision
test: «Ratings are decided by trained examiners who follow published rules.» Who decides the ratings? | The film makers | A machine that guesses | *Trained examiners who follow published rules | Friends and family
test: «A mediator is a trained helper who helps them agree.» In a custody case, what is a mediator? | *A trained helper who helps parents agree | A parent who lives far away | A child who decides where to live | A judge who gives a fine
exam: «The Coriolis effect is too weak to decide which way water drains from a bath.» What can the Coriolis effect not do? | Heat the bath water | *Settle which way water drains | Make water drain faster | Stop a bath from draining
